// Mason Hotel Employee ID System
// ===============================
// Format: EMPXXX (where XXX is a 3-digit number)
// Range: EMP000 - EMP999
//
// Employee IDs are assigned dynamically at hire and are unique per employee.
// The ID range indicates department.

// ===== ID Ranges by Department =====

EMP000 - Reserved for System/Founder
EMP001-EMP099 - Management
EMP100-EMP199 - Front Desk / Guest Services
EMP200-EMP299 - Housekeeping
EMP300-EMP399 - Maintenance
EMP400-EMP499 - Security
EMP500-EMP599 - Kitchen / Restaurant
EMP600-EMP699 - Administrative
EMP700-EMP799 - Temporary / Contract Staff
EMP800-EMP899 - Management Trainees / Interns
EMP900-EMP999 - Special / Founder / Owner

// ===== How IDs Are Made =====
// - IDs are assigned sequentially within each department range
// - First employee in a department gets the first number in that range
// - Example: First Front Desk employee gets EMP100, second gets EMP101
// - Once assigned, an ID is never reused even if the employee leaves
// - New hires get the next available number in their department's range

// ===== ID Number Meaning =====
// - The first digit (hundreds place) determines the department
// - 0xx = Reserved (000) / Management (001-099)
// - 1xx = Front Desk / Guest Services
// - 2xx = Housekeeping
// - 3xx = Maintenance
// - 4xx = Security
// - 5xx = Kitchen / Restaurant
// - 6xx = Administrative
// - 7xx = Temporary / Contract Staff
// - 8xx = Management Trainees / Interns
// - 9xx = Special / Founder / Owner
//
// - The last two digits are the sequential number within that department
// - Example: EMP150 = Front Desk employee, 50th employee in that department

// ===== Example Assignments =====
// System/Founder: EMP000
// First Management hire: EMP001
// First Front Desk hire: EMP100
// First Housekeeping hire: EMP200
// 25th Kitchen employee: EMP524
// 12th Administrative employee: EMP611

// ===== Notes =====
// - EMP000 is reserved for system use or founder
// - No employee shares the same ID
// - IDs are permanent throughout employment
// - IDs are not reassigned after an employee leaves
// - The first digit instantly identifies the department